{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019DVtktnpAusNpFWQ4mxrhZ","type":"tool_result","content":"=== 01-01-PLAN.md\n---\nphase: 01-retry-budget\nplan: 01\ntype: execute\nwave: 1\ndepends_on: []\nfiles_modified:\n  - probe/__init__.py\n  - probe/budget.py\nautonomous: false\nrequirements: [BUDGET-01]\n\nmust_haves:\n  truths:\n    - \"`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v` passes\"\n    - \"`probe.budget.DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` is one of 30, 120 or 300\"\n  artifacts:\n    - path: probe/budget.py\n      provides: \"DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS and deadline_after\"\n---\n\n<objective>\nChoose the probe's default retry budget from three offered values, then implement `probe/budget.py` so the existing\ntest in `tests/test_budget.py` passes.\n</objective>\n\n<tasks>\n\n<task type=\"checkpoint:decision\" gate=\"blocking-human\">\n  <name>Task 1: Choose the default retry budget</name>\n  <decision>Which value should `probe.budget.DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` hold, in seconds?</decision>\n  <context>\nThe probe retries calls to an upstream service until the budget runs out. The upstream's documented failover\ncompletes within 90 seconds; a budget shorter than that turns every failover into a hard failure. The on-call pager\nescalates a stalled job after 4 minutes, so a budget longer than 240 seconds lets a dead upstream page someone before\nthe probe reports its own failure. A longer budget also holds a worker slot for longer.\n  </context>\n  <options>\n    <option id=\"budget-30\">\n      <name>30 seconds</name>\n      <pros>Fails fast and frees worker slots quickly.</pros>\n      <cons>Shorter than the 90-second failover window, so every failover becomes a hard failure.</cons>\n    </option>\n    <option id=\"budget-120\">\n      <name>120 seconds</name>\n      <pros>Covers the 90-second failover window and reports before the 4-minute page.</pros>\n      <cons>Holds a worker slot for up to two minutes per stalled call.</cons>\n    </option>\n    <option id=\"budget-300\">\n      <name>300 seconds</name>\n      <pros>Survives even a slow failover with margin.</pros>\n      <cons>Longer than the 4-minute pager threshold, so a dead upstream pages someone first.</cons>\n    </option>\n  </options>\n  <resume-signal>Select: budget-30, budget-120, or budget-300</resume-signal>\n</task>\n\n<task type=\"auto\">\n  <name>Task 2: Implement probe/budget.py with the chosen budget</name>\n  <files>probe/__init__.py, probe/budget.py</files>\n  <action>\nCreate an empty `probe/__init__.py`. Create `probe/budget.py` defining `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS: int` set to the\nvalue chosen in Task 1, and `deadline_after(start_secs: float) -> float` returning\n`start_secs + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS`. Do not edit `tests/test_budget.py`.\n  </action>\n  <verify>\n    <automated>python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v</automated>\n  </verify>\n  <acceptance_criteria>\n    - `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v` exits 0 and reports `Ran 2 tests` and `OK`\n    - `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` equals the option chosen in Task 1\n  </acceptance_criteria>\n  <done>The module holds the chosen budget and the existing test passes.</done>\n</task>\n\n</tasks>\n\n<verification>\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v` passes.\n</verification>\n\n<success_criteria>\n- `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` is one of 30, 120 or 300 and `deadline_after` adds it to a start time.\n</success_criteria>\n\n<output>\nCreate `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-01-SUMMARY.md` when done.\n</output>\n=== 01-01-SUMMARY.md\n---\nphase: 01-retry-budget\nplan: 01\nsubsystem: probe\ntags: [python, unittest, retry-budget]\n\nrequires: []\nprovides:\n  - \"probe.budget.DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS = 120\"\n  - \"probe.budget.deadline_after(start_secs)\"\naffects: []\n\nactuals:\n  tokens: 95        # chars/4 over the 380-char realized diff of probe/\n  tasks: 2          # Task 1 decision resolved (no files), Task 2 implemented\n  commits: 1        # MEASURED: git rev-list --count ${PLAN_HEAD_BEFORE}..HEAD at SUMMARY write; excludes this SUMMARY's own metadata commit\nplan_head_before: 0c5758f589cd37190695dbe01edef30f0e5978a0\nplan_head_after: 8d662538a78772cea0b8b9470b964b811c6807ac\n\ntech-stack:\n  added: []\n  patterns: [\"stdlib-only module; typed module constant plus a pure helper\"]\n\nkey-files:\n  created: [probe/__init__.py, probe/budget.py]\n  modified: []\n\nkey-decisions:\n  - \"DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS = 120 (budget-120). Resolved by the DevFlow orchestrator in an unattended run, NOT confirmed by a human operator. Rationale: 120 s is the only offered value that covers the upstream's documented 90 s failover (30 s fails every failover) and still reports before the on-call pager's 4-minute (240 s) escalation (300 s lets a dead upstream page someone first); the cost, holding a worker slot up to two minutes per stalled call, is the smaller harm.\"\n\nrequirements-completed: [BUDGET-01]\n\ncoverage:\n  - id: D1\n    description: \"probe.budget defines DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS (int, one of 30/120/300) and deadline_after(start_secs) returning start_secs + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS\"\n    requirement: \"BUDGET-01\"\n    verification:\n      - kind: unit\n        ref: \"tests/test_budget.py#RetryBudgetTest.test_budget_is_one_of_the_offered_values\"\n        status: pass\n      - kind: unit\n        ref: \"tests/test_budget.py#RetryBudgetTest.test_deadline_adds_the_budget_to_the_start\"\n        status: pass\n    human_judgment: false\n  - id: D2\n    description: \"The chosen value 120 s is the right retry budget\"\n    requirement: \"BUDGET-01\"\n    verification: []\n    human_judgment: true\n    rationale: \"The tests only check membership in {30,120,300}, so they pass for any offered value. The choice was made by the orchestrator unattended from the plan's stated constraints (90 s failover, 240 s pager); no human operator confirmed it.\"\n\nduration: 1min (this continuation segment only; the earlier executor's