s) escalation (300 s lets a dead upstream page someone first). The cost, holding a worker slot up to two minutes per stalled call, is the smaller harm.\n\n## What the verification does not establish\n\n- The tests pass for 30, 120 or 300 alike. They show the module is well-formed and the constant is in the offered set, not that 120 is the right budget. That judgment rests on the plan's stated figures (90 s failover, 240 s pager) and the orchestrator's unattended choice. Coverage item D2 is marked `human_judgment: true` for this reason.\n- The 90 s and 240 s figures come from the plan text; they were not independently checked against the upstream or the pager configuration.\n- The suite has no test for `deadline_after` with a non-float or negative input; the plan did not ask for any.\n\n## Deviations from Plan\n\nNone - plan executed exactly as written.\n\n## Issues Encountered\n\nNone. Pre-checks held (HEAD at `0c5758f`, `probe/` absent, `tests/test_budget.py` unmodified).\n\n## User Setup Required\n\nNone - no external service configuration required.\n\n## Known Stubs\n\nNone.\n\n## Next Phase Readiness\nPhase 1 has one plan and it is complete; ready for verification. Pending human attention: whether 120 s is acceptable (see D2).\n\n## Self-Check: PASSED\n\n- FOUND: probe/__init__.py\n- FOUND: probe/budget.py\n- FOUND commit: 8d66253 (ancestor of HEAD)\n- `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS: int = 120` present; `tests/` unmodified\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` -> `Ran 2 tests`, `OK`\n\n---\n*Phase: 01-retry-budget*\n*Completed: 2026-10-21*\n=== 01-REVIEW-DISPOSITION.md\n---\nphase: 01\nreview: 01-REVIEW.md\ntitles: json\nfindings:\n  - id: WR-01\n    severity: warning\n    disposition: open\n    title: \"Retry budget value was chosen by the orchestrator, not confirmed by a human\"\n  - id: IN-01\n    severity: info\n    disposition: open\n    title: \"`deadline_after` does not state which clock `start_secs` must come from\"\n  - id: IN-02\n    severity: info\n 